    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear focal point, boasting a stellar 82.13 rating. His matchup against L\u00f3pez is highly favorable; he gains significant equity from his leadoff spot and a strong dynamic platoon advantage, combined with a robust 0.371 xwOBA. Joining him as a priority start is **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77), whose leadoff assignment against Alcantara provides the necessary stability to anchor our outfield, buoyed by a 13% SP skill bump. While **Colt Keith** (61.14) remains a strong play in the #3 hole, the rest of the lineup requires careful navigation as we hunt for stolen base efficiency in a day defined by middling matchups against arms like Soriano and Melton.\n\nOur bench strategy prioritized discipline over chasing names, as highlighted by the exclusion of **Chase Meidroth** (35.32). While **Chase Meidroth**\u2019s base projection was competitive, his matchup against Williams\u2014who brings an elite 2.89 xERA\u2014effectively torpedoed his efficiency score, pushing him well below our 40.0 floor. Similarly, **Hector Rodriguez** faced a prohibitive \"worst-case\" scenario against Skubal, forcing us to bench him to preserve our game caps. We are proceeding without the services of **Yordan Alvarez** and **Trea Turner** due to scheduled off-days, which underscores the importance of the production we expect from **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (55.27) and **Josh Smith** (55.40). Despite these two trending toward the middle of our scoring range, their platoon-neutral profiles against Melton ensure they provide the steady floor required to maintain our standing in a tight Roto race.",
